    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_77e7ad49d34caf52a727a6bacace9c675cbdb1c5dec66ee10d8f20b6f3bef2eb",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The passage localizes the theorem's range limitation to one unresolved auxiliary estimate: the other work nearly completes the proof, whereas this remaining term is available only with a trivial bound, so tightening that bound would widen the range of the asymptotic formula. This localization identifies where additional proof effort matters, but it neither explains the size of the trivial bound nor identifies the cancellation needed to improve it; those questions remain in the unreadable preceding formulas.",
